    {
      "filename": "Phatart Lampangluang Temple.jpg",
      "title": "File:Phatart Lampangluang Temple.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Phatart_Lampangluang_Temple.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phatart_Lampangluang_Temple.jpg",
      "width": 4256,
      "height": 2832,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Mr.Peerapong Prasutr",
      "description": "-Pra Thart Lam Parng Luang Temple is one of the most important temples of the Wang river basin. It is located at Lam Parng Luang village, Moo 2, Koh Kha District, Lam Parng Province.\n-The legend stated that during the Buddhist era Buddha come to meet Lua Aye Gon and predicted that there would be a person who built a city named Lampa Kuppa or Lam Parng City and Buddha's relics would be brought to be located here. Pra Thart Lam Parng Luang is the pagoda of the people who were born in the year of the\n\nOx. There is a worship ceremony every year in the 12th lunar month (Yi Peng). There is a bathing ceremony for Buddha's relics and the Emerald Buddha every year on 16 April. There is also a worship ceremony for Buddha’s footprints in the north on the 6th lunar month of every year. This temple is the temple that Buddhist people should not miss visiting.",
      "dateCreated": "2014-01-04 15:27:28",
